		(uuid "5911cbfe-2693-47a5-9645-fa7a870a2d1c")
	)
	(text "Half-Bridge Phase B\nGate drive + MOSFETs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 39.116 154.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.81 3.81)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f03ac56a-79c1-4f03-89a3-b90ea3fce912")
	)
	(text_box "The L6498D incorporates an internal bootstrap diode, thus it does not need an external one.\n\nIn order to make the design compatible with the NCP5183 gate driver, an external diode is added. Worst case it can be replaced by a 0 Ohm resistor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 220.98 0)
		(size 87.63 16.51)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "16d10dc2-2cf5-4c31-9886-7a291c5554ea")
	)
	(text_box "For the pull-down resistors at MOSFETs gates, datasheet suggests:\n\n\"The circuit guarantees less than 1 V on the LVG and HVG pins (at Isink = 10 mA), with V CC > 3 V. This allows omitting the \"bleeder\" resistor connected between the gate and the source of the external MOSFET normally used to hold the pin low.\"\n\nI am still putting the pull-down resistors for initial power-up state; DNP if unwanted"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 199.39 0)
		(size 87.63 20.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ccfdbfac-8bc7-45a9-b4f6-4c2ff159dbfd")
	)
